    "norm": "Verifies that a lone closing suffix ('}') in the template is treated as plain text and is NOT interpreted as part of a variable reference. <p>The template {@code \"The animal} jumps over the ${target}.\"} contains: <ul> <li>{@code animal}} – a closing suffix with no preceding opening prefix; it must be kept verbatim.</li> <li>{@code ${target}} – a well-formed variable that resolves to {@code \"lazy dog\"}.</li> </ul> The expected result is {@code \"The animal} jumps over the lazy dog.\"}."
